<p class="lead">The best bow sight for Mathews bows is the one that fits how you hunt and how your riser mounts a sight. Mathews changed the sight question when it added Bridge-Lock to its newer risers, and now you have more choices than ever: Bridge-Lock dovetail sights, conventional bracket sights, fixed pins, sliders and hybrids.</p>

<p>This Better Outdoors buying guide explains what Bridge-Lock is, which brands make compatible sights, how to choose between fixed pins and a single pin slider, what pin size to pick, and which features are worth paying for. It is a buying guide, not a test report: we focus on the features and trade-offs that should drive your decision.</p>

