<p>Fixed pins are the traditional whitetail choice for a reason. Deer appear fast, distances inside 40 yards are common, and you never want to fumble with a dial. A <?= amz('5 pin bow sight', '5 pin bow sight') ?> is simple, rugged and easy to sight in.</p>
<p>A single pin slider shines when you have time to range. Western hunters, 3D shooters and anyone shooting past 50 yards often prefer one pin and an exact sight tape. If that sounds like you, browse a <?= amz('single pin slider bow sight', 'single pin slider bow sight') ?> with a lockable elevation dial and clear tapes.</p>
