<h2 id="h-bow-sight-pin-size-010-vs-019">Bow Sight Pin Size: .010 vs .019 (and Everything Between)</h2>
<p>Pin diameter is listed in inches, usually .010, .019 or .029. The fiber optic is what you see glowing.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>.019</strong>: the middle ground most hunters choose. Bright enough at dawn and dusk without covering too much of a deer at 40 yards.</li>
  <li><strong>.010</strong>: very fine. Covers less of the target at long range, so it suits target shooters and long-range hunters, but it is dimmer in low light.</li>
  <li><strong>.029</strong>: the brightest and easiest to see in dark timber, but it covers more of the target farther out.</li>
</ul>
<p>Many sights mix sizes, such as a .019 top pin with .010 lower pins, so your close pin is bright and your long pins are precise. Longer fiber wraps also gather more light. Check your state&rsquo;s rules if you are considering a sight light, as some states restrict them during certain seasons.</p>

